      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5b7e2b17f8f0c04d194bf47e|full_name}: this was the physics method I was referring to. It does shake a lot with movement, which breaks the effect in some cases, and an additional issue is that child joints of the fixed joint still get local transformations, unless they have an explicit connection to the fixed joint. Additionally, having a joint be both free to move as well as in world space is impossible with this method. Worldspace objects should act more like worldspace particles, ideally.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-09-17T22:12:27.332Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It would be nice to have objects disconnected from parent transforms. People usually use the physics system to do this, but it's not ideal. Truly being able to remove parent transforms from an object would open up creative pathways for avatars. As far as I know, an official script to do this would be easy and not dangerous. Please give this to avatar creators.",
